From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: overdoingism <overdoingism@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 05:40:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cuda: mmvk v3, K-quant decode / verify matmul with the
 activations kept in registers, on by default

v3 = v2 with GGML_CUDA_MMVK=2 by default (0 turns it off; GGML_LF_ALL=0 makes it default to off; silent on a GPU it
does not run on).

For Q4_K / Q5_K / Q6_K weights at 1..8 columns (decode and speculative verify): one lane owns one 32-value sub-block,
loads the q8_1 activations of all columns for it once and runs several weight rows against them.  GGML_CUDA_MMVK=1
launches each MUL_MAT alone; =2 also launches the MUL_MATs that read the same input (gate + up, q + k + v, DeltaNet
qkv + z) as one kernel, weight types mixed (GGML_CUDA_MMVK_EXT bit 1, default on; bit 2 adds IQ4_XS / IQ4_NL / MXFP4).
1 and 2 run only when the program verifies speculative drafts: llama-server tells the backends through
"ggml_backend_set_speculative_decoding" before it loads the models (one-token decode alone is 1-1.6% faster on the
stock kernel); 3 and 4 are the same, always.  RDNA4 only.

Not bit-identical to MMVQ (float summation order); decode and verify give the same results as each other.  The fusions
that compute the matmul inside MMVQ (single-token GLU, bias) stand down for these types; the verify-band ones that only
pre-fill the q8_1 cache (add + rms_norm, rms_norm, GLU -> q8_1) stay.

Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q4_K_XL, DFlash2 n-max 5, gfx1201: -4.7% / -5.1% per step at 8K / 110K (=2), draft acceptance unchanged,
long-context KLD below the one-bit floor (Qwen3.8 Q5_K_M, Qwen3.6-27B Q4_K_M).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
